1.bug_scenario:
The user’s screenshot and GIF show that when formatting a JavaScript file containing a JSDoc `@satisfies` annotation on an object literal, Prettier drops the surrounding parentheses. Input code like:

  module.exports = /** @satisfies {Record<string, string>} */ ({ hello: 1337 });

gets reformatted to:

  module.exports = /** @satisfies {Record<string, string>} */ { hello: 1337 };

which removes the parentheses and breaks TypeScript intellisense. The bug is that JSDoc type‐cast comments other than `@type` aren’t recognized as needing parens, so the printer strips them.
